title: 'Transport failures are reported as ''Hetzner API error: 500'' with no reason'
updated: 2026-10-13T19:50:28Z
---

`WWW::Hetzner::LWPIO::call` (`lib/WWW/Hetzner/LWPIO.pm:52-70`) hands on only status and body of LWP's response. For a request that never reached Hetzner (connection refused, DNS, TLS failure, timeout, missing LWP::Protocol::https) LWP synthesises a 500/501 with a plain-text body; `_parse_response` (`lib/WWW/Hetzner/Role/HTTP.pm:253-261`) decodes only bodies that look like JSON and otherwise croaks with the bare status.

Reproduce:

    perl -Ilib -e 'use WWW::Hetzner::Cloud; eval { WWW::Hetzner::Cloud->new(token => "t", base_url => "http://127.0.0.1:9")->get("/servers") }; print $@'
    # Hetzner API error: 500 at lib/WWW/Hetzner/Cloud.pm line 179.

A network problem is indistinguishable from a real server error of the API, in the library and in `hcloud.pl`/`hrobot.pl`. The same applies to any non-JSON error body (a proxy's HTML 502/503): only the number survives.

Done when: LWPIO detects LWP's internal response (`Client-Warning: Internal response`) and the croak names the reason (`Hetzner API error: Can't connect to ...`); a non-JSON error body contributes its status line. Test in `t/io.t` with a stub UA.

